  "Number": 6,
  "Question": "The average cost of a long-distance call in the USA in \\(1985\\) was \\(41\\) cents per minute, and the average cost of a long-distance call in the USA in \\(2005\\) was \\(7\\) cents per minute. Find the approximate percent decrease in the cost per minute of a long-distance call.",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(7\\)",
    "B": "\\(17\\)",
    "C": "\\(34\\)",
    "D": "\\(41\\)",
    "E": "\\(80\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "Percent decrease measures the amount lost as a percentage of the original cost. The cost fell by \\(41-7=34\\) cents per minute, so the percent decrease is\n\\[\n\\frac{34}{41}\\cdot100\\%\\approx83\\%.\n\\]\nThe closest offered value is \\(80\\%\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{E}\\).",
